 "_note": "The two terrains, in the game's own X/Y where one unit is 100 m and Y counts north. Everything here is a measured position transcribed from wardogs-artillery.com, which calibrated its maps against in-game coordinates. Positions are the facts; the drawing is ours.",
 "_tiles": "The tiles block draws terrain imagery under the vectors. Shape: { path, tileSize, minZoom, maxZoom, extension, bounds }, where path is site-absolute and zoom Z is a 2^Z square of tiles spanning bounds, row 0 being the north edge, named zoom_<z>/<x>_<y>.<extension>. bounds is the calibration box in game coordinates and is not exactly the map extent, because the capture landed a few metres off the round number. Imagery is the game's own, re-encoded to lossy webp and cut to zoom 5, which is 2 m per pixel and 32 MB for both maps. We host our own copy rather than hotlink anyone.",
